The '''whipcord launcher'''<ref name="SW:AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> or '''whipcord thrower'''<ref name="CotR">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> was a piece of equipment that shot out a lariat, with the intention of tangling up opponents and preventing them from moving.<ref name="SW:AEYNTK" /> The [[bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett]] and his [[Cloning|clone]] son<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> [[Boba Fett]] both used whipcord launchers mounted on their [[Mandalorian vambrace]]s<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> that can release a [[fibercord whip]]. [[Cad Bane]] also had a whipcord launcher built into his right [[gauntlet]].<ref name="CotR" /> [[Grappling Trooper]]s of [[Death Watch]] used whipcords to capture and imprison enemies.<ref name="Friend">{{TCW|A Friend in Need}}</ref> Members of the [[Nite Owls]]<ref name="The Phantom Apprentice">{{TCW|The Phantom Apprentice}}</ref> and the bounty hunter [[Din Djarin]] also utilized whipcords.<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref>

While battling on [[Kamino]], Jango Fett used his whipcord launcher to drag [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] around on the platform they were fighting on.<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> Death Watch also used whipcord launchers in capturing [[Ahsoka Tano]] before tying her up for execution.<ref name="Friend" /> Cad Bane used his whipcord launcher to save Obi-Wan Kenobi who was disguised as [[Rako Hardeen]] in the [[Box]].<ref name="The Box">{{TCW|The Box}}</ref> Boba Fett used one to immobilize [[Luke Skywalker]] during the brawl on [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba's]] [[sail barge]].<ref name="Episode VI" /> Din Djarin used one of his whipcord launchers to ensnare Tano during their brief fight in the woods of [[Corvus]].<ref name="Chapter 13">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 13: The Jedi}}</ref>

